      "title": "Super Intelligence: Why Teams Need an AI-Augmented Operating System | Embracing Digital Transformation",
      "summary": "Super Intelligence: Why Teams Need an AI-Augmented Operating System | Embracing Digital Transformation Embracing Digital Home Guidance Briefings (EDTW) What changed Interviews (EDT) How others did it Architectural Deep Dives What to do next Learn Digital Transformation Overview Pillars AI, Cyber, Data, Edge, Computing, Comms ODXA Domains &amp; mappings Whitepapers Monthly canonical synthesis Articles Explainers &amp; analysis Lectures (DTA) Learning series Intelligence Community Community Newsletter Patreon LinkedIn About About Host Sponsors Shop Search Skip to content Home Episodes Episode 29: Super Intelligence: Why Teams Need an AI-Augmented Operating System Episode 29 Super Intelligence: Why Teams Need an AI-Augmented Operating System 2026-10-28 Hosted by Dr. Darren Pulsipher Explore more in the episode archive . Summary In this episode, Dr. Darren explores the concept of super intelligence as a shared capability formed when people and AI collaborate within an AI-Augmented Operating System (AAOS). He outlines how organizations can move beyond isolated AI experiments to responsible, repeatable AI-enabled work by connecting AI outputs to accountable workflows. The episode explains the six-stage AAOS cycle—Diagnose, Activate, Control, Execute, Measure, and Scale—and emphasizes the importance of clear boundaries, ownership, evidence, and continuous learning to create dependable AI-augmented operations. AI Artificial Intelligence Super Intelligence AI-Augmented Operating System AAOS Digital Transformation Workflow Automation AI Adoption Operational Accountability Team Collaboration Technology Leadership Continuous Improvement Copyright &copy; Paidar Productions LLC All rights reserved",
